//@ run-pass
//@ requires: madaros
// Engine-gated, not silenced. The CI suite runs souc-stage2, which is the
// lean_single self-host output, not Madaros -- see SOUNIO_TEST_SOUC_BIN in
// .github/workflows/ci.yml. The property under test is the Madaros parser rewriting extern declarations
// into forwarding wrappers. lean_single has no such rewrite, so the fixture
// would pass there for the wrong reason.
// Verified PASS on a Madaros built from this branch, on Slurm.
// A declared-but-never-called extern "C" with no backend intrinsic.
//
// check.sio's E250 design comment states this case is legal and names
// ffi_libm_call.sio as the fixture it protects: "Checked at the CALL, not at
// the declaration ... both compile and pass today, and a declaration-site
// refusal would break them for no gain."
//
// Measured 2026-08-23 on clean origin/main: rc=0, no diagnostic. The comment is
// accurate there. This fixture exists so it stays accurate, because the
// re-entrant parser in this branch rewrites EVERY declaration into a wrapper
// whose body calls ffi_<name>, and an unbound ffi_<name> then fails with E137
// inside the wrapper before the call-site rule is ever consulted.
//
// The name is deliberately one no allowlist will ever carry.
extern "C" {
    fn zzz_no_backend_intrinsic_exists(x: i64) -> i64;
}

fn main() -> i32 with IO, Panic {
    println("ffi_declared_never_called_is_legal: PASS")
    return 0
}
